  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4103.17 Footwear or leather care product",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4103.17 “Footwear or leather care product” means any product designed or labeled to be applied to footwear or to other leather items or components, to maintain, enhance, clean, protect, or modify the appearance, durability, fit, or flexibility of the footwear or leather item or component. The term does not include fabric protectant, general purpose adhesive, contact adhesive, vinyl/fabric/leather/polycarbonate coating, rubber/vinyl protectant, fabric refresher, products solely for deodorizing, or sealant products with adhesive properties used to create external protective layers greater than 2 millimeters thick.\n\nSource. #10527, eff 2-26-14; ss by #13969, eff 5-21-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4100.html"
